<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area rose slightly in the week ending Oct 31, an industry source said. The following are estimated levels, with week-ago and year-ago levels.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>		31/10/96		24/10/96		3/11/95</p>
<p> gasoline    400		    400-425		 400</p>
<p> naphtha	75		     75			50</p>
<p> gas oil    1700-1725	     1650-1700	    2050-2100</p>
<p> fuel oil    400		     350		    625</p>
<p> jet	    15			10		     20</p>
<p>Moga was quiet. Incoming coasters, outgoing barges Naphtha-Incoming coasters outgoing barges to German petrochemical industry. Gasoil-Active. Incoming cargoes from CIS, Mediterranean and United States. Outgoing to Benelux, Germany and Switzerland. Fuel oil-Incoming straight run from CIS, outgoing to bunkers. JP1-Incoming for blending for gasoil.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
